# CareerAI Chrome Extension Context

## Project Type
- Chrome Extension (Manifest V3) built with React + TypeScript and bundled with webpack.
- Runtime surfaces: popup UI, options page, background service worker, and content script overlay.

## Core Entry Points
- `src/popup/popup.tsx`: popup auth gate + popup detail page.
- `src/options/options.tsx`: minimal options surface.
- `src/background/background.ts`: external login/logout message bridge to chrome storage and tabs.
- `src/contentScript/contentScript.tsx`: injects React app (`JobDetector`) into pages.
- `src/static/manifest.json`: extension metadata, permissions, content script, background worker.

## State and Data Flow
- Redux Toolkit store in `src/store/store.tsx` with root reducer in `src/store/rootReducer.tsx`.
- Main slices: `AuthSlice`, `JobDetailSlice`, `ResumeListSlice`.
- API calls and async logic are split into feature API files under `src/store/features/**`.
- Auth/token is synced via `chrome.storage.local` and axios interceptor (`src/config/axiosInstance.tsx`).

## Feature Architecture
- `src/landingPage/DetectJob/JobDetector.tsx` is the central orchestrator for content-script UI.
- `src/jobExtractor/*` handles per-site job detail extraction.
- `src/autofill/*` handles domain-specific form filling flows.
- `src/page/**` contains page-level React screens (`resumeList`, `jobDetail`, `profile`, `popupDetail`).
- `src/component/**` contains shared UI building blocks.
- `src/hooks/**` contains site observers and behavior hooks.

## Build and Environment
- webpack config: `webpack.common.js`, `webpack.dev.js`, `webpack.prod.js`.
- Build output is `dist/` and static assets are copied from `src/static`.
- Environment toggles and backend URLs live in `src/config/urlconfig.ts`.

## Working Conventions For Agent
- Prefer targeted edits; avoid broad refactors unless requested.
- Preserve existing naming/style patterns in nearby files.
- For extension behavior changes, consider all 4 surfaces: content script, popup, background, manifest.
- When touching extraction/autofill, preserve website-specific condition checks and selectors.
- Keep Redux action/state naming consistent with existing slice patterns.

## Exploration Constraints
- Do not inspect or modify `dist/`.
- Do not inspect or modify `node_modules/`.
- Focus code reading and edits on source/config files only.
